    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Junior Caminero** (70.80) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (64.80) serving as our primary offensive anchors. **Junior Caminero** benefits from a high-upside matchup against Alcantara, whose 4.46 xERA suggests vulnerability to high-exit-velocity hitters. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** remains a priority despite a lower spot in the order; his elite sprint speed and aggressive baserunning profile against Martin provide a high floor for the scarcity-heavy stolen base category. **Luke Raley** (62.62) also merits attention as a sneaky start, as he faces a favorable platoon split against Buehler, and the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery cadence creates an optimal environment for **Luke Raley** to secure a stolen base.\n\nWhile we are starting a deep lineup, the most difficult decision involved **Hyeseong Kim** (47.00), who narrowly missed the cut. Despite his strong contact profile, the optimizer relegated **Hyeseong Kim** to the bench due to a combination of an unfavorable #9 lineup spot and a challenging matchup against Soriano\u2019s 3.75 xERA. Conversely, we are keeping **Casey Schmitt** (63.92) in the active lineup on the assumption he bats #3 against Severino; the projected platoon advantage and favorable park factors provide enough leverage to override the risk of his pending official lineup status.\n\nThe primary risk today lies in the top of the order, specifically regarding **Yordan Alvarez** (54.65), who faces the formidable deGrom. While **Yordan Alvarez** maintains an elite 0.425 xwOBA, the 3.11 xERA of the opposing starter significantly depresses his daily efficiency score. Similarly, **Trea Turner** (59.13) faces a stiff test; while his #1 lineup position is a massive positive, his stolen base upside is mitigated by a catcher exchange (1.89s pop time) that forces us to temper expectations for his total contribution. We will monitor the status of **Casey Schmitt** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** closely, as any deviation from their projected lineup slots could necessitate further adjustments to our daily allocation.",
